{"run_id": "20260816T231526-hepkg-48570", "qid": "gen-concept-5e5b6b9c", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "92159134c9c3", "git_sha": "be3072a-dirty", "question": "Count the analyses that estimate the background Charge-flip electron background.", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 33 analyses that estimate the background \"Charge-flip electron background\" or related backgrounds.\n\nThis includes 67 distinct facts and 72 assertions. \n\nTo provide more context, here are the specific backgrounds that were considered:\n- Charge-flip electron background\n- Electron sign mismeasurement (charge misID) background\n- Material-conversion electron background (Mat Conv)\n- Misidentified-hadron peaking background (electron channel)\n- Charge-misassignment (QMisID) background\n- W->l nu background (W->tau nu decays and electron charge misidentification)\n- Zγ (photon conversion) background\n- Photon conversion background (Zg, Wg, ttg)\n- $V\\gamma$ background\n- W/Z+γ background\n- Dileptonic $t\\bar{t}$ background (2$\\ell$OS channel)\n- Xγ (photon conversion, mainly Zγ) irreducible background\n- Fake/non-prompt lepton background\n- $VV$ (diboson) background\n- Resonant background leakage (J/psi, psi(2S) radiative tail)\n- Fake lepton background\n- Non-prompt and fake-lepton background\n- Diboson ($VV$) background\n- t̄t+γ background\n- Non-resonant WW diboson background\n- $t\\bar{t}H$ background\n- Nonprompt lepton background, multilepton channel\n- Continuum non-resonant diphoton background in the $m_{\\gamma\\gamma}$ spectrum\n- Central diffraction background\n- Nonprompt lepton background\n\nThese backgrounds are related to the charge-flip electron background in various ways, such as being part of the same category or being mentioned in the same context in the papers.\n\nIf you need more detailed information on any specific background or analysis, let me know!", "answered": true, "pa